Package: DietView
Title: Interactive, Hierarchical Visualization of Stomach-Content Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = c("Sosthène", "A. V."), family = "Akia",
           email = "akiasosthene@gmail.com",
                      role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("CADI Gulf Center", role = "fnd"))
Description: Builds interactive, hierarchical views of predator diet from a
    long table of stomach-content records, one row per prey record. Prey are
    placed in a taxonomic hierarchy either by querying the World Register of
    Marine Species ('WoRMS'; WoRMS Editorial Board <doi:10.14284/170>)
    through 'worrms', with a per-prey log of how each name was matched, or by
    joining a lineage table supplied by the user. Records identified only to a
    coarse rank are kept and shown as an explicit unidentified category below
    that rank, so every ring of the resulting sunburst accounts for all the
    material examined. Diet is summarized as shares of prey records, numbers
    and weight at every rank, alongside the classical frequency of occurrence.
    Further functions describe how identification depth changes with
    digestion state, draw prey accumulation curves, aggregate rare prey to a
    stated stomach-frequency threshold and export sample-by-prey matrices for
    multivariate analysis. Results can be explored in a 'shiny' application,
    drawn as 'plotly' figures or written to a single self-contained HTML file.
